1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,819
Every few months somebody predicts
something about the future, and it keeps
landing on the same year.

2
00:00:05,059 --> 00:00:06,093
Twenty twenty-seven.

3
00:00:06,553 --> 00:00:11,314
AI timelines, disclosure files,
geopolitics — different conversations
sharing a date.

4
00:00:11,654 --> 00:00:17,796
We're not going to tell you what happens,
because nobody knows, and we'd rather ask
the question than pretend we have the
answer.

5
00:00:18,096 --> 00:00:20,849
That's what VIRUS2027 is built on.

6
00:00:21,269 --> 00:00:24,869
And this is Vira, who notices the pattern
in the noise before the rest of us.

7
00:00:25,269 --> 00:00:29,855
Underneath the mystery, the mechanics are
deliberately boring, and all of it is on
the chain.

8
00:00:30,135 --> 00:00:34,525
It runs on Pulse prediction markets, so
what you think about the future has
somewhere to go.

9
00:00:34,985 --> 00:00:37,029
Follow the signal, and remember the date.
